Sval: an animated drop-shadow filter blurs smoothly

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 1766397 (mozilla-central 2443cf3b5b39,
Firefox 158), adapted: ESR 153's FrameBuildingContext has no
max_surface_size(), so the size cap is read the way ESR's picture.rs
reads it, max_surface_override or MAX_SURFACE_SIZE. The commit's three
regenerated wrench reference PNGs are left out: ESR 153's references
differ from the ones it replaced.
WebRender downscales a large blur before blurring it, and the downscale
grid moved with the surface's inflation, which tracks the blur radius.
An animated drop-shadow therefore shifted against its content every
frame and visibly pulsed. The source is now aligned to the downscale
grid of the largest blur in device space.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 158.

